# Curated art and architecture: styles grouped into families, the monuments that define each style,
# and which styles shaped which. Hand-written from the Wikipedia articles each row names; build.py pins
# every monument to Wikidata (id, coordinates, inception) and flags dates that disagree.
#
# A style is precise (Gothic, Ottoman imperial mosque); a family is the coarse grouping the map colours
# by (Christian medieval, Islamic). A monument may belong to more than one style.
#
# STYLES: slug -> dict(name, family, start, end, origin=(lat, lon, place name), wd=[Wikidata style ids
#   that map to this style], what, why, spread, approx)
# MONUMENTS: (slug, enwiki title, styles, start, end, what, extra) ; extra may hold place= (an existing
#   kernel place id to reuse instead of a new record), kind='artwork', approx=True, causes=[...].

